{"acceptance_length": 6.113636363636363, "acceptance_lengths": [2, 4, 4, 11, 5, 5, 4, 3, 10, 9, 6, 3, 1, 2, 7, 4, 2, 3, 8, 1, 1, 14, 2, 7, 4, 5, 8, 2, 16, 13, 2, 5, 5, 3, 11, 4, 15, 13, 8, 16, 6, 3, 8, 4], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 21690740736, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 21690735616, "benchmark": "math500", "completion": "We are told that the **sale price** of a shirt is **$14.40**, and this is **60% off** the **original price**. We are asked to find the **original price** of the shirt.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand what \"60% off\" means\n\nIf the shirt is **60% off**, that means the **sale price** is **40% of the original price** (because 100% - 60% = 40%).\n\nSo:\n\n$$\n\\text{Sale Price} = 40\\% \\text{ of Original Price}\n$$\n\n$$\n14.40 = 0.40 \\times \\text{Original Price}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Solve for the original price\n\nLet the original price be $ x $.\n\n$$\n14.40 = 0.40x\n$$\n\nNow divide both sides by 0.40:\n\n$$\nx = \\frac{14.40}{0.40}\n$$\n\n$$\nx = 36\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{36}\n$$\n\nThe original price of the shirt was **$36**.", "decode_seconds": 1.7635679109953344, "draft_calls": 44, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 66, "method": "native_target_dflash", "output_hash": "3451ddcc43e902a5bde296ff7645e0fbc84823b72032c4fbc580af75c7e0369f", "output_tokens": 268, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 21788332544, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 22118662144, "problem_id": "math500/488", "profile_regions_ms": {"unattributed_runtime": 1805.770797189325}, "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "\\$36", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 1.805770797189325, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 22118662144, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 22118662144, "target_calls": 44, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.03322869120165706, "turn_index": 0}
