ntegers less than 2010.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Count how many of these have reciprocals with terminating decimals\n\nWe want to count how many **odd integers less than 2010** have **reciprocals with terminating decimals**.\n\nAs we said earlier, this happens **if and only if** the number is of the form:\n\n$$\nn = 2^x \\cdot 5^y\n$$\n\nBut since we are only considering **odd integers**, the power of 2 must be 0. So:\n\n$$\nn = 5^y\n$$\n\nSo we are looking for **odd integers less than 2010**", "decode_seconds": 3.7034235722385347, "draft_calls": 98, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 81, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "b4562dc664748ec2da6e0f1ccac13820bfd0fa9c413a7a3235ebec5f1d84b613", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "01f46ab3e5986b3dd56cffe01f5c74b09e886a1d1aeb68dc9ea4dede5c47f077", "output_tokens": 512, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 21870448128, "peak_reserved_memory_bytes": 22118662144, "problem_id": "math500/482", "profile_regions_ms": {"draft": 508.6706566810608, "prefill_full_target": 33.69228744506836, "prefill_relay": 0.22684800624847412, "relay": 25.64444798231125, "unattributed_runtime": 38.674421701580286, "verification_full_target": 3132.4222469329834}, "proposal_lengths": [15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15], "rank": 0, "reference_answer": "202", "repetition": 0, "request_seconds": 3.7393309087492526, "reserved_memory_after_bytes": 22118662144, "reserved_memory_before_bytes": 22118662144, "target_calls": 98, "time_to_first_token_seconds": 0.033999832812696695, "turn_index": 0}
